 established in 2012-03-24. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Conservative People's Party of Estonia (EKRE), founded on March 24, 2012, in Tallinn, emerges from the complex post-Soviet political landscape of Estonia. This nationalist political entity champions traditional values, national sovereignty, and skepticism toward the European Union, positioning itself as a significant player in Estonian politics. EKRE's establishment reflects a broader trend in European politics where conservative and nationalist sentiments have gained traction in response to globalization and immigration issues.

